From 7de5d6b7af91c0dd75e7ac53aa1892bfa58fbba1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Spanier <spanier.michael@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 16:01:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/34] usb_webcam: give every camera its own node

With two cameras plugged in, only the first one could be used. The flavor
was not global, so an application that instantiated it loaded the add-on
itself, counted the cameras anew and got internal ids that did not match
the flavor it had asked for. The producer also allowed only one instance
for the whole add-on.

Mark the flavor B_FLAVOR_IS_GLOBAL so the node lives in the
media_addon_server, and drop the instance counter: each camera has its
own flavor with possible_count 1, so the media kit already makes at most
one node per camera. The add-on keeps a list of its nodes and tells each
of them when a camera is plugged in.

A camera plugged in again used to get a new internal id, so the media
server made a second node for it and the old one was left without a
camera. CamFlavorIds remembers the ids of unplugged cameras by name and
gives the old id back. Tests in CamFlavorIdsTest.

